{"name":"Morning Tea","hex":"#cabd94","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"morning tea","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small meal or snack eaten between breakfast and lunch; a period of time set aside for this purpose, taken as a break from schoolwork, work, a conference, etc."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/morning_tea"}],"entries":[{"title":"Elevenses","blocks":[{"text":"Elevenses is a short break taken at around 11:00 a.m. to consume a drink or snack. The names and details vary among countries."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/SLNSW_13120_A_movie_set_three_women_and_a_man_take_morning_tea_scene_from_These_Children_BritishAustralian_production.jpg/330px-SLNSW_13120_A_movie_set_three_women_and_a_man_take_morning_tea_scene_from_These_Children_BritishAustralian_production.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elevenses","wikidata":"Q2915067"},{"title":"Morning","blocks":[{"text":"Morning is either the period from sunrise to noon, or the period from midnight to noon. In the first definition it is preceded by the twilight period of dawn, and there are no exact times for when morning begins because it can vary according to one's latitude, and the hours of daytime at each time of year. However, morning strictly ends at noon, when afternoon starts."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg/330px-Morning%2C_just_after_sunrise%2C_Namibia.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morning","wikidata":"Q7722"},{"title":"Tea","blocks":[{"text":"Tea is an aromatic beverage prepared by infusion of hot or boiling fresh water with fresh or cured leaves of Camellia sinensis, an evergreen shrub native to East Asia that originated in the borderlands of southwestern China, northeast India and northern Myanmar. Tea has a stimulant effect in humans primarily due to its caffeine content."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d3/Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg/330px-Longjing_tea_steeping_in_gaiwan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tea","wikidata":"Q6097"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg/500px-Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg/1280px-Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ee/Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg/500px-Albert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"1884 painting by Albert Edelfelt, titled Elevenses","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAlbert_Edelfelt_-_Elevenses_-_A_III_1976_-_Finnish_National_Gallery.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/1280px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a4/Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg/500px-Floris_Claesz._van_Dyck_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org